From 6e5b6c9bc3bac27796451e65189e58341d2d2062 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 11:28:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08527/11362] Fix LocalGGUFProposer leaking a stale
 llama-server child (2026-08-08 review, Correctness #4)

_ensure_server left a still-loading llama-server child running and
referenced on wait-exhaustion timeout; the next call found the server
unhealthy, skipped reuse, and Popen'd a second child on the same port,
overwriting self._proc -- so stop() could only ever reach the newest
child, and the orphan (eventually holding real VRAM) became unreachable
by any cleanup path. Found in the 2026-08-08 adversarial review
(docs/research-notes/live-agent-adversarial-review-2026-08-08.md,
Correctness finding 4).

Adds LocalGGUFProposer._terminate_stale_proc(reason): if self._proc is set
and still alive, sends SIGTERM, waits up to 5s, escalates to SIGKILL if
needed, then always clears the reference. Wired in at both sites the
review named -- immediately before the Popen that would otherwise
overwrite self._proc, and right after wait-exhaustion before returning
failure. Records a cleanup event on its own diagnostic channel
(orphaned_child_cleanups -> liveness_witness()["generator_orphaned_child_
cleanups"]), separate from n_server_failures, so a leak-from-a-prior-
attempt cannot spuriously flip a liveness gate for a run whose eventual
server is healthy -- matching the existing reasoning for reuse_refusals.
stop() itself is unchanged; the review cited it only as evidence of the
reachability problem.

5 new tests in test_arc_ensure_server_leak_fix_20260808.py: wait-exhaustion
terminates the child and clears self._proc; a live prior child is
terminated before a replacement launch; an already-dead prior child is
left alone; no prior child is a clean no-op; SIGKILL fires when SIGTERM
doesn't reap in time. Adversarially verified independently -- the
verifier wrote its own standalone harness (fully mocked Popen) to
confirm BOTH the wait-exhaustion path AND the reuse-miss path reach the
fix, since the shipped tests only directly exercised the former.
CONFIRMED_FIXED. Re-verified myself -- 9/9 pass (own file + regression
against test_arc_generator_stderr_capture.py), --no-cov, targeted files
only.

First patch-apply attempt for this fix produced a real syntax error (an
off-by-one in a hand-split zero-context patch inserted new lines one
statement too early inside a try/except block). Caught immediately by
ruff/mypy in pre-commit before anything was committed; re-split with full
context instead of zero-context and re-verified syntax, tests, and lint
clean before this commit.

Adds REQ-ARC-WMTE-6221 to the openspec capability (already present from
the prior commit's spec batch). 7 results/*.json artifacts get a
freshness_acknowledgements entry: this fix changes resource cleanup on a
future server-restart edge case, not any already-recorded game outcome,
model output, or measured value.

Confirmed disjoint from the conductor's own in-progress, uncommitted
REQ-ARC-WMTE-6213 work in the same file (object-delta-perception, lines
~2939-2963/3060) -- untouched, left exactly as found.

